From 6c5ee57c5cbe589ca56cdc641d421af828b38f43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:27:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: ease the page, status bar and button row through the
 tab sheet close

Two things still changed in a single frame while the bottom tab sheet closes.

At the hand-off the page card was restored at once: the page's translation
snapped back from its parked offset, its clip, corner radius, scrim, shade and
backdrop were cleared, the status bar colour was restored, and the compositor
toolbar layer came back in the same pass, so the page and the top toolbar
jumped. On the close path the parked page translation, scale, corner radius,
scrim, shade and backdrop are now held at the values they had before the park
and eased to the restored state over the existing hand-off fade. The status
bar colour is eased the same way, and the compositor toolbar layer stays
suppressed until the ease has finished, so the restored toolbar views are what
cross-fade in.

At the start of the close the five-button row, with the plus button and its
tonal highlight, was gated behind the first part of the sheet's travel and then
appeared at full strength in one frame. On the close path the row's travel is
now latched when the close starts and eased from that value across the whole
close, so it fades and slides in continuously. The open path, the settled bar,
the cover and travel easing from the previous patch, and everything after the
close chrome is finished are unchanged.

The unit tests cover the page translation, backdrop and status bar being
continuous across the hand-off and easing monotonically to the restored state,
a reopen in the middle of the fade, the open path keeping its immediate page
shift, and the button row fading in from the first frame of a close from half
and from a partial pull, while opening keeps its threshold.
